        "client_msg_id": "57c030eb-eed1-4ff9-aa00-c6710df294da",
        "text": "Love it.  Probably the most exciting thing about coding agents as such is how they can help lower the bar for bespoke one-offs.  For instance instead of just describing an orrery with text, I wanted an interactive one with both reasonable table-top scale for the earth, sun, and moon as well as a realistic scale so you could really see and *feel* how small the sun and moon are in the sky.  Really cool, but without assistance not worth the effort.",
        "team": "T5TCAFTA9",
        "thread_ts": "1769384610.270969",
        "parent_user_id": "U08294YLWJH",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "ZqO2A",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "Love it.  Probably the most exciting thing about coding agents as such is how they can help lower the bar for bespoke one-offs.  For instance instead of just describing an orrery with text, I wanted an interactive one with both reasonable table-top scale for the earth, sun, and moon as well as a realistic scale so you could really see and "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "feel",
                                "style": {
                                    "bold": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " how small the sun and moon are in the sky.  Really cool, but without assistance not worth the effort."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "user": "U0887QU9G2V",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1769460578.572349",
        "client_msg_id": "dd160557-7b10-4713-bb64-81ea6227aff3",
        "text": "I wrote a short <https://federicopereiro.com/writing-syntax/|article> prompted by Ryan Dahl\u2019s statement that \u201cthe era of humans writing code is over.\u201d (I consider Ryan a living legend, BTW).\n\nI have two objections/doubts:\n1. What if code is no longer writing \u201csyntax\u201d? What if code can be as readable as natural language?\n2. How are we supposed to review code if we don\u2019t write it? Can you be an editor without being a writer? Can we consider LLMs as good enough code writers that take natural language descriptions of a system, in the same way we consider compilers \u201cgood enough\u201d machine code generators?\nI\u2019d like to hear what you think (or feel) about this.",
        "team": "T5TCAFTA9",
        "thread_ts": "1769460578.572349",
        "reply_count": 6,
        "reply_users_count": 3,
        "latest_reply": "1769545578.721139",
        "reply_users": [
            "U05GSC0B4A0",
            "UJBAJNFLK",
            "U0887QU9G2V"
        ],
        "is_locked": false,
        "subscribed": false,
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "WWKaj",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "I wrote a short "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "https://federicopereiro.com/writing-syntax/",
                                "text": "article"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " prompted by Ryan Dahl\u2019s statement that \u201cthe era of humans writing code is over.\u201d (I consider Ryan a living legend, BTW).\n\nI have two objections/doubts:\n"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_list",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "rich_text_section",
                                "elements": [
                                    {
                                        "type": "text",
                                        "text": "What if code is no longer writing \u201csyntax\u201d? What if code can be as readable as natural language?"
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "rich_text_section",
                                "elements": [
                                    {
                                        "type": "text",
                                        "text": "How are we supposed to review code if we don\u2019t write it? Can you be an editor without being a writer? Can we consider LLMs as good enough code writers that take natural language descriptions of a system, in the same way we consider compilers \u201cgood enough\u201d machine code generators?"
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ],
                        "style": "ordered",
                        "indent": 0,
                        "border": 0
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\nI\u2019d like to hear what you think (or feel) about this."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
